      "text": "Problem:\nTo find the area of figure \\(ABCD\\), we need to determine the area of the two sectors placed side by side. The circle has a radius of 12, and each sector is \\(60^\\circ\\).\n\n1. **Calculate the area of one sector:**\n   - The area of a full circle is given by \\( \\pi r^2 \\).\n   - Substituting the radius \\(r = 12\\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of one full circle} = \\pi \\times 12^2 = 144\\pi\n     \\]\n   - Since each sector is \\(60^\\circ\\), a sector is \\(\\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{6}\\) of the full circle.\n   - Therefore, the area of one sector is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of one sector} = \\frac{1}{6} \\times 144\\pi = 24\\pi\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total area of the figure \\(ABCD\\):**\n   - There are two sectors, so the total area is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total area} = 2 \\times 24\\pi = 48\\pi\n     \\]\n\nThus, the area of figure \\(ABCD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{48\\pi}\n\\]",
