      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the area of figure \\(ABCD\\) formed by two sectors of a circle of radius 12, with each sector having a central angle of \\(60^\\circ\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the area of one sector:**\n\nA sector of a circle is a fraction of the circle’s area. The area \\(A\\) of a sector with a central angle \\(\\theta\\) (in degrees) of a circle of radius \\(r\\) is given by:\n\\[\nA = \\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi r^2\n\\]\n\nFor our problem:\n- Radius \\(r = 12\\)\n- Central angle \\(\\theta = 60^\\circ\\)\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\\[\nA = \\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} \\times \\pi (12)^2\n\\]\n\nSimplify the fraction:\n\\[\nA = \\frac{1}{6} \\times \\pi \\times 144\n\\]\n\nFurther simplification:\n\\[\nA = \\frac{144\\pi}{6} = 24\\pi\n\\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of two sectors:**\n\nSince there are two sectors forming figure \\(ABCD\\), we multiply the area of one sector by 2:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of figure } ABCD = 2 \\times 24\\pi = 48\\pi\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of figure \\(ABCD\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{48\\pi}\n\\]",
